# The guardrail guards itself. Changes to the policy, the detectors, the workflows and
# the hooks are exactly the assets a bypass would target, so they require a code-owner
# review — the human half of the sign-off model in SPEC §5.4. Pair this with branch
# protection ("Require review from Code Owners") or it is advisory only.
# `src/` as a whole, not just the detectors: the gate job builds the CLI from the PR's
# own head, so `engine.ts`, `cli/`, `git/`, `diff/` and `signoff.ts` decide the verdict
# as surely as a detector does — a `hasBlocking` that returns false is a bypass with no
# detector touched. `package.json` carries the build and test scripts the gate runs and
# the version that triggers a release; the lockfile pins what those scripts execute.
/.tamperward.yml        @hexrift
/.github/               @hexrift
/.husky/                @hexrift
/src/                   @hexrift
/package.json           @hexrift
/package-lock.json      @hexrift
/tsconfig.json          @hexrift
